  "question": {
    "text": "Evaluate: $\\int \\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{x}}{4-\\mathrm{x}^{3}}} \\mathrm{dx}$"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{3} \\sin ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x^{3 / 2}}{2}\\right)+c$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{3} \\sin ^{-1}\\left(x^{3 / 2}\\right)+c$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$2 \\sin ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x^{3 / 2}}{2}\\right)+c$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{3} \\sin ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{x}^{3 / 2}}{2}\\right)+\\mathrm{c}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$I=\\int \\sqrt{\\frac{x}{4-x^{3}}} d x=\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{x} d x}{\\sqrt{4-x^{3}}}$\r\nHere integral of $\\sqrt{x}=\\frac{2}{3} x^{3 / 2}$ and $4-x^{3}=4-\\left(x^{3 / 2}\\right)^{2}$\r\nPut $x^{3 / 2}=t \\Rightarrow \\sqrt{x} d x=\\frac{2}{3} d t$\r\nSo $I=\\frac{2}{3} \\int \\frac{d t}{\\sqrt{4-t^{2}}}=\\frac{2}{3} \\sin ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x^{3 / 2}}{2}\\right)+c$"
  }
}